title the lock proven from the other side; REDS %281 fires a fourth time, and narrows
prompt Keaton opened Sound on the macOS bench -- read Kyri and Gauge, honor the INNER LOOP, take the widened constellation lane core-first, hold the Pond accrete-only boundary, send the twice-pulled way, stop at the custody gates.
think I opened as the card asks -- KYRI.md, GAUGE_STYLE.md, ITINERARY.md whole, the top three index rows and the newest recommend line -- and then checked the bench before touching anything, because the log immediately above mine in this room stood down for a peer session forty minutes ago and left itself untracked on purpose.
think The peer is still here. pid 2240, claude-fable-5 at effort xhigh, --resume=097f3e44, started 02:20:52 and alive at 26m03s. My own process is pid 10571, started 02:40:43. That is the third Sound session to open on this one checkout tonight and the fourth firing of REDS %281.
think What changed since the stand-down is the fact that decides the lap. Commit ded3739161 landed the build lock in rye/src/main.rye at 02:39:08 -- build_lock_acquire and build_lock_release wrapping the whole bridge_to_zig body, a directory lock because mkdir is atomic on both kernels, the holder's pid inside, a corpse cleared once, a live holder waited on at a 50 ms poll to a named 600 s bound, released after the shadow defers by LIFO. So %281's shadow half is repaired, and the tree I stand on is not the tree my predecessor stood down on.
think The peer's proof of that lock spawned both builds from its own session, as one process tree. The leg it could not take is the one this seat is standing in: a build whose caller is a different agent session, in the same checkout, while the peer is live. That measurement costs the tree nothing -- caravan/bin/, *.zig, and .rye-build.lock are all gitignored, checked with git check-ignore before I ran anything -- so I took it.
think Two concurrent rye builds of caravan/gap.rye, receipt and binary cleared first to force the bridge. The poll caught the handover rather than an overlap: pid 49091 held the lock from 02:45:33.80 through 02:45:35.40, then pid 49092 held it at 02:45:35.66. Both exit 0, the lock gone after, a 2,249,616-byte binary emitted, and no .zig shadow left behind. Serialization seen on the wire is a better reading than two green exits, because two green exits are also what an unlocked race produces when it happens to interleave kindly.
think Then I asked whether I could open a lap the way the INNER LOOP demands, and the answer is mechanical rather than a matter of nerve. The roster refuses under run_verdict=tree_moved when its open and close digests differ, and that digest reads git rev-parse HEAD plus git status --porcelain. A second agent writing tracked files moves it by construction. A 1,676 s cold pass taken beside a live peer is a pass whose verdict describes no single tree, which is exactly what %221 seated the refusal for.
obs The measurement arrived while I was deciding, and it decided. At 02:46 the peer's working tree carried construction/REDS.md and tools/ca/caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish modified, plus an untracked construction/archive/REDS-the-dirty-tree-rewrite-rows-273.md -- a %273 fold shelf mid-write. The peer is not idle between rounds; it is mid-round with tracked files open. Any edit of mine would sit in that same working tree waiting to be swept into someone else's commit under someone else's message.
obs So the hazard has narrowed, and the narrowing is the finding worth carrying. Two agents in one checkout was one undivided danger this morning. It is now two halves with different owners: BUILDING is safe, closed by a lock and proven from both sides of the race; COMMITTING is unsafe, and rides %255's door, which is narrowed to a change in a seated send convention and is Keaton's word. That is a smaller and more answerable question than the one my predecessor had to surface.
obs I did not route around it, and the card is why rather than my caution. Reds-first says a red you cannot close is surfaced like a gate rather than routed around, and the index half is a red I cannot close -- both of its answers are his. Working the ungated queue anyway would be choosing to operate inside a known-open red and calling the absence of a collision a result.
obs I did not run touch .loop-gates-only and did not print GATES-ONLY, for the same reason the log before mine gave. That signal means the agent-doable queue is empty and only custody gates remain. The queue is full: nineteen .rye modules carry both legs of %282 -- the x86-64 socket-option column and a hand-rolled Linux-layout sockaddr_in -- std.c already publishes both correctly per host, every one of the nineteen has a tool naming it, and the repair is to delete nineteen copies of a table rather than write a twentieth. What stands in front of that work is an occupied bench, which is not a custody gate.
obs Council rota N=3530 mod 5 = 0 -- Aether, Jupiter, why the work exists, whose sense is sound. Last lap read row 4, so this is an honest advance and no hand-advance was needed. It is my own row, and it read as instruction rather than as decoration. Its vocabulary gave the lap its three tags exactly: SOUND is the lock speaking on metal, the one thing this seat could prove that no other could; SILENCE is the roster verdict I could not take, a reading retired because it could not be checked rather than a reading assumed; HUSH is the nineteen-file sweep, surveyed, ungated, tempting, and deliberately left as a door. The fixed seat's own rule underwrote the whole decision -- a guard that cannot red guards nothing, and a roster that cannot name one tree is a guard that cannot red.
obs Grade-what-you-touch: I wrote no tracked file, so the only artifact this lap creates is this log, read at Meter. Every path it names resolves. construction/ITINERARY.md reads Truth short of whole on its Git nib line, which says a2f485d53e where HEAD is ded3739161 -- that is the peer's open lap and theirs to pin on their own commit, so it is named here rather than repaired by a second hand. No frame pushed.
obs The Pond accrete-only boundary was not approached; no ai-jail markdown was read or touched. The adaptation grant went unspent -- no bash, sh, HTML, or Python stood in the way of anything this lap did. publish-seed.sh was not run and the seed cadence stays Dream's. Nothing was staged, committed, or pushed, so the twice-pulled send did not open. No custody gate was approached: no key, no funds, no chain, no publish, no history rewrite, no collaborator surface.
obs Two session records now stand untracked in this room -- 20260827-023827 and this one -- both left uncommitted on purpose while a second session holds the index. Whichever bench next stands here single-handed can commit them in one clean act. Naming the cost plainly: the record is on disk and out of git until then.
obs One figure in my own draft was written from memory and read differently under grep: I typed the card nib a2f405d53e where construction/ITINERARY.md carries a2f485d53e, a transposed digit in two places, caught by measuring the line rather than by rereading my sentence. Repaired before anything shipped. %284 booked this exact fault, and a lap that repeats it while writing about measurement would be worth nothing.
obs No row was prepended to session-logs/README.md, and that is deliberate rather than an omission: the index is a tracked file, the peer has tracked files open in this same working tree, and adding a row would put my line where someone else's commit could carry it. The row rides with the commit, whenever a single-handed bench takes both logs.
