recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the bench carries two agents and %281 has fired four times, yet the question is now half its old size. The BUILD half is closed: the lock landed in rye/src/main.rye at ded3739161, and this lap proved it from the second session -- two concurrent builds of caravan/gap.rye handing the lock 49091 to 49092 at 02:45:35.66, both exit 0, no shadow left. The COMMIT half is what remains, it rides %255, and both its answers are still yours: put the nib amend behind an explicit check that HEAD moved, or give each aether star its own checkout. Until one is picked, a full roster taken beside a live peer refuses under tree_moved by its own design, so a second session cannot honestly open a lap here. Ungated and fully surveyed for whichever bench stands here alone: nineteen .rye modules carry BOTH legs of %282, std.c already publishes both per host, and each closes on a witness that already names it.
